WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.967
Fine-tuning is useful when you have a stable behavior you want the model to learn repeatedly and prompting or rag does

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:10.382
not solve it reliably.

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:17.027
Examples include specialized classification, a consistent response format, or a domain-specific behavior.

00:00:17.027 --> 00:00:21.622
Frequently changing facts are usually better handled through retrieval.

00:00:21.622 --> 00:00:27.722
A useful test is to ask whether the missing capability is behavior or knowledge.

00:00:27.722 --> 00:00:34.671
Fine-tuning is better suited to stable behavior; rag is better suited to changing external knowledge.
